# 1. Purpose

This document defines the minimum and recommended system requirements for developing, deploying, and testing the Open Smart Register Platform (OpenSRP) within the Open Oncology Care Platform (OOCP).

It establishes a consistent development baseline to ensure contributors work in reproducible environments and reduce environment-specific issues.

---

# 2. Scope

This document applies to:

* Local development
* Docker deployments
* Testing environments
* Continuous Integration (CI)
* Future production deployments

---

# 3. Supported Operating Systems

## Recommended

* Ubuntu 24.04 LTS (or current supported LTS release)

## Supported

* Ubuntu 22.04 LTS
* Debian 12+
* Fedora (latest stable)
* macOS (Apple Silicon and Intel)
* Windows 11 using WSL2 (Ubuntu)

Linux is the preferred development platform because it most closely matches typical production deployments.

---

# 4. Hardware Requirements

## Minimum

| Component | Requirement        |
| --------- | ------------------ |
| CPU       | 4 cores            |
| Memory    | 8 GB RAM           |
| Storage   | 100 GB SSD         |
| Network   | Broadband Internet |

---

## Recommended

| Component | Requirement                   |
| --------- | ----------------------------- |
| CPU       | 8 cores or more               |
| Memory    | 16 GB RAM or higher           |
| Storage   | 250 GB SSD or NVMe            |
| Network   | Reliable high-speed broadband |

---

## Production (Future)

Expected production infrastructure will be sized according to:

* Number of healthcare facilities
* Concurrent users
* Patient population
* Synchronisation frequency
* Availability requirements

